{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-70649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+5)^{2}+{z}^{2}=10?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can write our equation as\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+(y-(-5))^{2}+{z}^{2}=(\\sqrt{10})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point point $C(0,-5,0)$ and the radius $r=\\sqrt{10}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40c9b47f84a46075b258520c8bb344da4c894b0d0c5fd9f11b282ef313c0163f"} {"question" "q-70649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$r=10$ and $C(0,0,-5)$"] ["text" "$r=10$ and $C(0,5,0)$"] ["text" "$r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $C(-5,0,0)$"] ["text" "$r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $C(0,-5,0)$"] ["text" "$r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $C(0,5,0)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $C(0,-5,0)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the radius $r$ and the coordinates of the center $C$ for the sphere $(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2}=4?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the equation of a sphere centered at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ with radius $r>0$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-{x}_{0})^{2}+(y-{y}_{0})^{2}+(z-{z}_{0})^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe can write our equation as\n\n$$\n(x-(-2))^{2}+{y}^{2}+(z-3)^{2}={2}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich gives us the center at the point point $C(-2,0,3)$ and the radius $r=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70648" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivaria