 of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(z+2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(z+2)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70927" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40c9b47f84a46075b258520c8bb344da4c894b0d0c5fd9f11b282ef313c0163f"} {"question" "q-70927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4"] ["math" "(x-2)^{2}+(z+2)^{2}=16"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4"] ["math" "{y}^{2}+(z+2)^{2}=12"] ["math" "{y}^{2}+(z-2)^{2}=12"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70927" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x-2)^{2}+(z+2)^{2}=16"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the projection of the intersection between the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2}=16$ and the plane $x=2$ onto the $yz$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the sphere and the plane $x=2$, we substitute $x=2$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2)^{2}+(y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 4+(y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =12 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{3})^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProjecting this onto the $yz$-plane gives us the circle of radius $2\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(-4,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70926" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "40c9b47f84a46075b258520c8bb344da4c894b0d0c5fd9f11b282ef313c0163f"} {"question" "q-70926" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70926" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "The circle of radius $12$ centered at $(0,0)$"] ["text" "The circle of radius $2$ centered at $(0,-4)$"] ["text" "The circle of radius $2\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(-4,0)$"] ["text" "The circle of radius $4$ centered at $(4,0)$"] ["text" "The circle of radius $\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(0,4)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-70926" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The circle of radius $2\\sqrt{3}$ centered at $(-4,0)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-71949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the projection of the intersection between the sphere ${x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+(z+1)^{2}=36$ and the plane $z=3$ onto the $xy$-plane." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-71949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the intersection of the sphere and the plane $z=3$, we substitute $z=3$ into the equation of the sphere:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+(3+1)^{2} & =36 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2}+16 & =36 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =20 \\\\ {x}^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{5})^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nProjecting this onto the $xy$-plane gives us the equation of the circle of radius $2\\sqrt{5}$ centered at $(0,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042177/state.json" "file_sha256" "d94aeaff82090a7938a0d72149a5f134f48e63b50ea71550611d24627b4ff4ab"} {"question" "q-71949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" 